 2. 👀 Top names for AI czar 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Photo: Alex Grimm/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump's announcement this weekend that he's forming an "AI Force," modeled on the Space Force he launched in his first term, caught advisers by surprise, Axios' Maria Curi reports. 

 Officials and executives inside and outside the administration are now jockeying to be Trump's AI czar, which he said he'll name soon. The czar will likely be a seasoned surrogate with Silicon Valley ties who can spearhead an AI rebranding effort, sources tell us. 🦾 Among the names to watch: 

 Scott Kupor, director of the Office of Personnel Management. Kupor has a degree in public policy and was Andreessen Horowitz's first employee. Sriram Krishnan, former senior White House AI policy adviser. Krishnan also worked at a16z and carried the torch for former AI czar David Sacks inside the White House after he left. Chamath Palihapitiya, Social Capital founder, CEO of 8090 and co-host of the All-In Podcast with Sacks and others. Sean Cairncross, White House national cyber director. Cairncross played a role in the administration's handling of the release of Anthropic's Mythos. Emil Michael, Pentagon CTO and under secretary for research and engineering. If the AI Force is housed in the Pentagon, Michael, who's also a former Uber executive, would be an easy fit. Keep reading . 

 
 
