 4. 🌐 AI breaks search 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Similarweb. Chart: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals Traffic to news sites is plummeting in the U.S. as tech giants steer people away from search and toward AI, Axios' Kerry Flynn and Sara Fischer report in an Axios Media Trends Executive briefing. 

 By the numbers: U.S. web traffic to roughly 100 of the top news sites fell to 47.6 million visits in July — down from peaks above 70 million in 2024, according to Similarweb data. Chatbot referrals have surged from 10,000 in July 2023 to more than 160,000 this July, but that remains a fraction of the traffic traditional search provides. 🔎 The intrigue: 2024 was the last big traffic year before the digital tides started turning on publishers.

 That was when Google introduced AI overviews within its search results and Meta rolled out a heavily expanded version of its Meta AI assistant. Share this chart ... Subscribe to Axios Media Trends Executive . 

 
 
