 7. 🤖 Resisting robots 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 "Pulling the Plug." Cover: Barry Blitt for The New Yorker The New Yorker's new cover (above) is cartoonist and illustrator Barry Blitt's take on the rising fears about AI and the threat it could pose to humanity. He writes : 

 "As a dedicated hypochondriac, I've had a number of pretty good conversations with Google's Gemini chatbot, about all manner of ailments. But I understand that AI may not always be looking out for my well-being." 
 
